b/ref 1071 "What is the volume of a rectangular solid that has length, width, and height of $2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m},$ $4\\,\\text{m},$ and $3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m},$ respectively?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540046 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3d05a680-5939-5ca9-9607-1df6158bf7b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540046 #edb/ref 1074 "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m},\\,w=4\\,\\text{m},\\,h=3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}=24\\sqrt{6}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540071 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186539960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540071 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118872" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540071 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540071 #edb/ref 1071 "A person has seven identical boxes in the form of a rectangular solid. Each box is $10\\,\\text{in}$ long, $8\\,\\text{in}$ wide, and $8\\,\\text{in}$ high. What is the total combined volume of the boxes?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540071 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "90edfdf5-24c3-54cd-8862-63c978f95f47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540071 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find the volume of one box.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=10,\\,w=8,\\,h=8\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=10\\cdot 8\\cdot 8=640\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total volume of the seven storage boxes is\n\n$$\n640\\cdot 7=4\\,480\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540102 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186539930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540102 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118873" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540102 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540102 #edb/ref 1071 "A shipping company delivered six identical packages in the form of a rectangular prism. Each package is $40\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $20\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $10\\,\\text{cm}$ high. What is the total combined volume of the packages?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540102 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e195bf20-65ce-5bd5-85a8-c18879f5cecb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540102 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find the volume of one package.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=40,\\,w=20,\\,h=10\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=40\\cdot 20\\cdot 10=8\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total volume of the six packages is\n\n$$\n8\\,000\\cdot 6=48\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
